{"content":[{"c":["DAN-JAAN"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Geographical landmark denoting the northern limit of David’s kingdom (",{"href":"?bref=2Sam.24.6","r":"2Sam.24.6","rawR":"2Sam.24.6","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Sam.24.6","value":"2Sam.24.6"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Sm 24:6"},"). Joab’s census taking stopped here. Some think this is a copyist’s error, because no town with a similar name is known to have existed in that area. Others believe that it means “Dan in the wood,” referring simply to Dan (see ",{"c":["rsv"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"},"). Still others think it refers to a town within Dan, perhaps Jaan, of which all traces have vanished."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"DanJaan","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"2 Sm 24:6","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Sam.24.6","rawQueryValue":"2Sam.24.6","sourceRefExact":"2Sam.24.6"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"a85c4ace28578012a6f97e5d9b6372a6b89c3bb74236af787fddc02c62e724d6","sourceItemName":"DanJaan","sourceItemOrder":21,"sourceMember":"Articles/D.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"DanJaan","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Dan-Jaan","title":"Dan-Jaan","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}